
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Git and GitHub Project</title>
</head>
<body>

    <h1>Git Repository Project</h1>

    <h2>1. Initialize Repository</h2>
    <pre>git init</pre>

    <h2>2. Add HTML File</h2>
    <pre>git add index.html</pre>

    <h2>3. Commit Changes</h2>
    <pre>git commit -m "First commit"</pre>

    <h2>4. Show Commit History</h2>
    <pre>git log</pre>

    <h2>5. Undo Commit</h2>
    <pre>git reset --soft HEAD~1</pre>

    <h2>6. Add Remote Repository</h2>
    <pre>git remote add origin https://github.com/USERNAME/MyProject.git</pre>

    <h2>7. Check Remote</h2>
    <pre>git remote -v</pre>

    <h2>8. Push to GitHub</h2>
    <pre>
git branch -M main
git push -u origin main
    </pre>

    <h2>Result</h2>
    <p>Git repository created successfully.
       Commit history displayed and project pushed to GitHub.</p>

</body>
</html>

